WEBVTT

1
00:01.333 --> 00:04.500
Your agent is waiting.
And you're not at your desk.

2
00:04.967 --> 00:07.667
Termote
Your Terminal, Anywhere.

3
00:07.867 --> 00:15.167
Two commands. One QR code.
Install, start on your network, scan it with your phone.

4
00:15.367 --> 00:22.333
A real terminal, built for thumbs.
Any shell, any CLI agent. Keys for Esc, Ctrl and arrows; swipe left for Ctrl+C, right for Tab.

5
00:22.533 --> 00:32.500
Chat with Claude Code and Codex.
Send the next message, see that it works, answer its questions with one tap.

6
00:32.700 --> 00:39.667
See exactly what changed.
Browse the files, preview Markdown and diagrams, review the agent's diff.

7
00:39.867 --> 00:42.167
Send files from your phone.
Upload with a button, a drop or a paste.

8
00:42.167 --> 00:44.167
Deleted by mistake?
It waits in the trash: restore it, or delete it for good.

9
00:44.367 --> 00:49.333
Herdr or tmux. Every agent, one place.
Herdr workspaces with each agent's status, or your tmux sessions: the same Chat, Files and Changes.

10
00:49.533 --> 00:54.333
Panes side by side.
Split, zoom, swap and resize them from the Pane menu, on tmux, Herdr and Zellij.

11
00:54.533 --> 00:56.667
Run the project's tasks.
npm, make, Go, Gradle, Maven, Cargo and more: one tap, in a tab of its own.

12
00:56.667 --> 00:58.833
Tiếng Việt, too.
The whole app in English or Vietnamese, picked in Settings.

13
00:59.033 --> 01:01.833
Get pinged when it's done.
A push when an agent finishes or needs you.

14
01:01.833 --> 01:04.667
Share a view-only device.
A one-time code pairs a tablet or a teammate's phone, without the password.

15
01:04.867 --> 01:09.167
Private by default.
Listens on 127.0.0.1 by default · Password or paired devices · View-only role · Tailscale HTTPS · Signed releases

16
01:09.433 --> 01:14.667
Your Terminal, Anywhere.
curl -fsSL https://termote.ohnice.app/install.sh | sh
termote.ohnice.app · Open source, MIT
